(* ======================================================================================
   validate/smeftfr_shim.fr
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Glue that lets the BOSONIC dimension-eight Lagrangian files shipped with SmeftFR v3.03
   (external/smeftfr_3_03/lagrangian_dim8_fr_files/2[1-8]_*.fr, Murphy classes 1 to 8) be
   evaluated inside OUR model, so that validate/fr_compare.wls can diff them vertex by
   vertex against the blocks emitted by dim8auto.

   HOW TO LOAD
   -----------
   This is a FeynRules model fragment.  It must be handed to LoadModel TOGETHER with our
   base model and the generated fragment, and it must come AFTER tests/gen_smoke/base.fr:

       Get["tests/fr_env/fr_headless_init.m"];
       LoadModel["tests/gen_smoke/base.fr", "tests/gen_smoke/gen.fr",
                 "validate/smeftfr_shim.fr"];

   validate/fr_compare.wls does this when its second argument names this file after gen.fr,
   separated by a comma:

       wolframscript -file validate/fr_compare.wls tests/gen_smoke/base.fr \
           tests/gen_smoke/gen.fr,validate/smeftfr_shim.fr validate/smeftfr_by_class/class2.m

   This file itself pulls in the eight SmeftFR bosonic Lagrangian files at the end, so the
   LQ... block definitions named in validate/smeftfr_pairs.m exist after LoadModel returns.
   SmeftFR is not shipped with this repository.  The eight files are 21_X4.fr to
   28_Xphi4D2.fr of the directory lagrangian/ of SmeftFR v3.03 (arXiv:2302.01353,
   www.fuw.edu.pl/smeft).  Copy them to external/smeftfr_3_03/lagrangian_dim8_fr_files under
   the repository, or set SMEFTFR$Dir to the directory that holds them (section 6).

   WHAT IS AND IS NOT ALIASED
   --------------------------
   Everything the eight bosonic files touch is listed here.  The complete set of symbols
   they use is: B, Wi, Gl, Phi8, Phi8bar, Ta, f, dSUN, Eps, FS, DC, del, HC,
   ExpandIndices, FlavorExpand, SU2W, SU2D, SMEFT$WB, SMEFTGaugeRules, Module,
   ToExpression, I.  Of those, B / Wi / Ta / f / dSUN / Eps / SU2W / SU2D and all the
   FeynRules primitives already exist in tests/gen_smoke/base.fr with IDENTICAL meaning,
   so only Gl, Phi8, Phi8bar, SMEFT$WB and SMEFTGaugeRules need defining.  Nothing in the
   bosonic files requires SmeftFR's own definitions/smeft_fields_WB.fr.

   CONVENTION AUDIT
   ----------------
   * SU(2) generators.  Both models declare
         SU2L: Representations -> {Ta,SU2D},
               Definitions -> {Ta[a_,b_,c_] -> PauliSigma[a,b,c]/2, FSU2L[i_,j_,k_] :> I Eps[i,j,k]}
     verbatim, i.e. Ta = sigma/2 and "2 Ta" = Murphy's tau in both.  No factor of 2 anywhere.
   * SU(3) structure constants.  Both declare StructureConstant -> f and
     SymmetricTensor -> dSUN.  Same names, same normalisation.
   * Higgs doublet.  Both give it FlavorIndex -> SU2D and QuantumNumbers -> {Y -> 1/2}.
     SmeftFR's Phi8[1] -> GP, Phi8[2] -> (vev + H + I G0)/Sqrt[2]; ours is the unitary
     gauge truncation Phi[1] -> 0, Phi[2] -> (vev + H)/Sqrt[2].  Because the alias below
     routes Phi8 onto OUR Phi, both sides of every pair use the same truncation, so the
     comparison is a unitary gauge comparison on both sides and is self-consistent.  It
     does NOT test the Goldstone sector.
   * Dual field strength.  SmeftFR writes Xtilde as Eps[mu,nu,al,be]/2 HC[FS[X,al,be]]
     with the two free indices FIRST; our generator writes (1/2) Eps[mu,nu,rho,sig]
     FS[X,rho,sig], also free indices first.  Identical, including the index order, so
     the Levi-Civita sign convention cancels between the two sides and epsLorSign never
     enters.  HC[FS[X,...]] = FS[X,...] for every real gauge field.
   * Covariant derivative sign.  THIS IS THE ONE REAL DIFFERENCE, and it is handled by
     NOT touching it.  FeynRules builds DC as del[f,mu] - I FR$DSign g A f and
     FS[X,mu,nu,a] as del[X[nu,a],mu] - del[X[mu,a],nu] + FR$DSign g f[a,b,c] X[mu,b] X[nu,c]
     (feynrules ToolBox.m:335-337, Core/ClassDeclarations.m:2110-2119).  Our base.fr sets
     FR$DSign = -1, which is Murphy's D = d + i g A.  SmeftFR never assigns FR$DSign
     anywhere in its package, so SmeftFR itself runs at the FeynRules default
     FR$DSign = +1, i.e. D = d - i g A, which is A -> -A relative to Murphy.
     The eight bosonic files contain no compensating signs: they are literal
     transcriptions of Murphy's table entries in terms of DC and FS.  Loading that text
     into OUR model therefore evaluates it with Murphy's derivative and Murphy's field
     strength, which is exactly the operator we want to compare against, so the shim adds
     NO sign correction.  Consequence to keep in mind: this validates the SmeftFR file as
     a transcription of Murphy, it does not reproduce SmeftFR's own published Feynman
     rules.  If you ever want the latter, set FR$DSign = +1 and every operator with an
     ODD number of explicit field strengths flips sign, i.e. all 6 of class 5 and all 6
     of class 8; classes 1, 6, 7 have an even number and classes 2, 3, 4 have none.
   * Wilson coefficient names.  SmeftFR builds them as SMEFT$WB <> <operator name>, with
     SMEFT$WB = "c" (code/smeft_variables.m:27), so the 89 bosonic coefficients are
     cG4n1 ... cBphi4D2n2.  They already carry 1/Lambda^4 inside their numerical value
     (code/smeft_initialization.m:210,248 sets Lam -> 1), whereas our blocks carry an
     explicit 1/Lam^4.  fr_compare.wls substitutes Lam -> 1 on the generated side, so the
     two normalisations agree with no extra factor.
   ====================================================================================== *)


(* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(* 1. Wilson coefficient prefix.                                                        *)
(*    Every SmeftFR operator block ends in ToExpression[SMEFT$WB <> "<name>"], so this   *)
(*    string is what turns the block into cG4n1 * (operator).  "c" is SmeftFR's own      *)
(*    default, set in code/smeft_variables.m line 27; keeping it means the coefficient   *)
(*    names quoted in validate/smeftfr_pairs.m are the ones SmeftFR itself would emit.   *)
(* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
SMEFT$WB = "c";


(* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(* 2. Gauge fixing replacement list.                                                    *)
(*    Every SmeftFR block finishes with "/. SMEFTGaugeRules".  In SmeftFR this is        *)
(*    SMEFTGaugeRules = If[!SMEFT$RxiGaugeStatus, {G0|GP|GPbar -> 0}, {}]                *)
(*    (code/smeft_io.m line 180), i.e. drop the Goldstones unless R-xi gauge was asked   *)
(*    for.  Our base.fr uses exactly the same construction under the name                *)
(*    feynmangaugerules (base.fr lines 730, 736), keyed on FeynmanGauge instead of on    *)
(*    SMEFT$RxiGaugeStatus, so we mirror it.  SetDelayed, not Set, so that flipping      *)
(*    FeynmanGauge after loading still does the right thing.                             *)
(*    With base.fr's FeynmanGauge = False this evaluates to {G0|GP|GPbar -> 0}, which is *)
(*    a no-op here because our Phi already has the Goldstones projected out, but it must *)
(*    be defined or the SmeftFR blocks return unevaluated ReplaceAll expressions.        *)
(* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
SMEFTGaugeRules := If[Not[FeynmanGauge], {G0|GP|GPbar -> 0}, {}];


(* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(* 3. Field aliases.                                                                    *)
(*    These are plain OwnValues, deliberately Set and not SetDelayed, so that the symbol *)
(*    is replaced at read time and FS / DC see OUR field in the head position.  A rule   *)
(*    list applied afterwards would not work: FS[Gl,mu,nu,a] has to be FS[G,mu,nu,a]     *)
(*    already when FeynRules resolves it against the SU3C gauge group.                   *)
(*                                                                                       *)
(*    Gl:  SmeftFR calls the SU(3) gauge boson Gl and reserves G for the PHYSICAL gluon  *)
(*         (definitions/smeft_fields_WB.fr lines 42, 196-201, where Gl[si,a] -> Gnorm    *)
(*         G[si,a]).  Our base.fr uses the single name G for both (GaugeBoson -> G,      *)
(*         ClassName -> G).  We have no dim-6 induced kinetic renormalisation, so their  *)
(*         Gnorm is 1 and the alias is exact.                                            *)
(*    Wi, B: same names in both models, nothing to do.  Note SmeftFR carries Wnorm and   *)
(*         AZnorm[i,j] in the Wi and B definitions where we carry the plain SM rotation; *)
(*         those constants are 1 at dim-4 and only differ once dim-6 operators are       *)
(*         switched on, which they are not here.                                         *)
(*    Phi8/Phi8bar: SmeftFR keeps TWO Higgs doublets, Phi (carrying the Hnorm, G0norm,   *)
(*         GPnorm renormalisations, used in their SM and dim-6 files) and Phi8 (with no  *)
(*         normalisation constants at all, used in every dim-8 file) -- see              *)
(*         definitions/smeft_fields_WB.fr lines 392-406.  The un-normalised Phi8 is the   *)
(*         one that corresponds to our Phi, so that is what we alias.  Phibar is the     *)
(*         antifield FeynRules generates automatically from base.fr's S[11].             *)
(* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
Gl      = G;
Phi8    = Phi;
Phi8bar = Phibar;


(* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(* 4. The Lorentz indices al, be, ga, de of the SmeftFR sources.                        *)
(*    Five SmeftFR blocks contract Lorentz indices named al, be, ga, de, which are       *)
(*    Global` symbols there: LQG4n8 (al,be,ga,de), LQG4n9 (ga,de), LQG2W2n7 (ga,de),     *)
(*    LQW2phi4n4 (al,be) and LQWBphi4n2 (al,be).  The blocks need these four symbols to  *)
(*    have no value.  Neither tests/gen_smoke/base.fr nor tests/gen_smoke/gen.fr uses    *)
(*    them, and they are cleared here, so that a value left in an interactive kernel     *)
(*    does not enter the five operators.                                                 *)
(* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
ClearAll[al, be, ga, de];


(* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(* 5. The 89 SmeftFR bosonic Wilson coefficients.                                       *)
(*    fr_compare.wls forms Coefficient[block, wc] and then calls FeynmanRules on the     *)
(*    difference, so the coefficient has to be a declared parameter of the merged model  *)
(*    rather than a free symbol.  A separate BlockName keeps them out of our DIM8 block. *)
(*    Value -> 1 rather than 0 on purpose: if anything ever did substitute numerical     *)
(*    values, a zero would turn every test into a false PASS.                            *)
(*    All 89 are declared, including the two class 3 coefficients whose operators are    *)
(*    deliberately NOT paired (see validate/smeftfr_pairs.m), so that the class 3 blocks *)
(*    can still be evaluated by hand when investigating that mismatch.                   *)
(* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
M$Parameters = {
  (* SmeftFR class 1 (X^4 and X^3 X-prime): 43 coefficients *)
  cG4n1 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 1,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_G4n1" },
  cG4n2 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 2,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_G4n2" },
  cG4n3 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 3,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_G4n3" },
  cG4n4 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 4,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_G4n4" },
  cG4n5 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 5,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_G4n5" },
  cG4n6 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 6,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_G4n6" },
  cG4n7 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 7,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_G4n7" },
  cG4n8 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 8,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_G4n8" },
  cG4n9 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 9,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_G4n9" },
  cW4n1 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 10,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_W4n1" },
  cW4n2 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 11,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_W4n2" },
  cW4n3 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 12,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_W4n3" },
  cW4n4 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 13,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_W4n4" },
  cW4n5 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 14,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_W4n5" },
  cW4n6 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 15,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_W4n6" },
  cB4n1 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 16,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_B4n1" },
  cB4n2 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 17,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_B4n2" },
  cB4n3 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 18,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_B4n3" },
  cG3Bn1 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 19,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_G3Bn1" },
  cG3Bn2 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 20,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_G3Bn2" },
  cG3Bn3 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 21,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_G3Bn3" },
  cG3Bn4 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 22,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_G3Bn4" },
  cG2W2n1 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 23,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_G2W2n1" },
  cG2W2n2 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 24,
    Value -> 1, InteractionOrder -> {NP,2}, Description -> "SmeftFR WC for Q_G2W2n2" },
  cG2W2n3 == { ParameterType -> External, BlockName -> SMEFTFRD8, OrderBlock -> 25,
